   "area_id": "co_mt_blue_sky_formerly_mount_evans_mixed_couloirs",
   "peak": "Mt. Blue Sky (formerly Mount Evans)",
   "peak_lat": 39.5886,
   "peak_lng": -105.643,
   "peak_elev": null,
   "parent": "Mt. Blue Sky (formerly Mt. Evans)",
   "pitches": 0,
   "approach": "The summit road (Highway 5) is seasonal and closed in winter, so in the cold months the approach adds a long walk up the road or in from Echo Lake via the Chicago Lakes basin. From the Summit Lake parking area, the Crystal is a narrowing couloir below the northwest face, just right of The Snave. It sits in morning shade, so the snow stays firm longer than on the sunnier couloirs of the bowl. Crampons and an axe are the standard kit. These are steep snow slopes in avalanche terrain, so check the avalanche forecast first.",
