   "peak_elev": null,
   "parent": "Mt. Blue Sky (formerly Mt. Evans)",
   "pitches": 0,
   "approach": "The summit road (Highway 5) is seasonal and closed in winter, so in the cold months the approach adds a long walk up the road or in from Echo Lake via the Chicago Lakes basin. From the Summit Lake parking area, walk to the east end of the lake and climb into the Summit Lake bowl. The snowfield is straight ahead, a broad slope between The Snave and the Diamond Couloir, and it is not always continuous up to the ridge. It is moderate snow, with crampons and an axe. These are steep snow slopes in avalanche terrain, so check the avalanche forecast first.",
