   "pitches": 0,
   "approach": "Start at the Bear Lake trailhead and take the trail to Emerald Lake, roughly 1.7 to 1.8 miles one way. At the shore, look left for the climbers' trail, then climb it up and right, contouring above the lake to the base of the big rock buttresses. Continue along the cliff base, then turn right and work up the gorge, staying slightly left of its middle to the obvious base of the couloir. The approach to the end of Tyndall Gorge is long. Snow slopes below the face can slide, so check the avalanche forecast.",
